    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "be the value of y predicted by the model, then the residual error is the deviation between the observed and predicted y value, i.e., $ e = y - \\hat{y} $. When information on x is used to predict y, x is referred to as the predictor or independent variable and y as the response or dependent variable.",
      "source_page": 55,
      "printed_page": 35,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter3:p005:b9"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        49.0,
